Collect the stadiums.

AWAYER is a personal log of visits to J.League grounds. Wins, rainy away days, and every pitch you stood in stay on your map.

Leave the day where it happened.
Open a pin and add the date, the match, a note, and up to 3 photos. Add another visit every time you go back. Season tickets and first away trips belong in the same book.

The map becomes your travel log.
Visited stadiums light up in the club colors. Places you have not been stay dark. Switch to the list to search by stadium or club. Pick a region from Hokkaido to Okinawa and the map zooms in.

Fill the league.
J1, J2, and J3. The progress board shows how far you have come. Filter by All-time, 2026, 2025, or Before 2025. Grounds is the number of different stadiums. Visits counts repeat trips too.

Former homes stay on the page.
Stadiums of clubs that left the J.League are marked Legend. They appear in All-time and Before 2025, and they are not part of the 60 for 2025 or 2026.

Your own stadium history.
A chart shows which grounds make up your travels—and which regions you have not stood in yet.

Share only what you have done.
The share image shows visited stadiums only. Unvisited pins are left out.

Records stay on this device.
There is no account. Dates, matches, notes, and photos are not sent to a developer server. Export a JSON file to move them, or import a file to replace what is on the device. Delete everything from Settings when you are done.

The dark pins are your next trip.
